From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Bruno=20Magalh=C3=A3es?= <brunom@tuta.io>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:19:09 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia: keep the VirtualMemory in DevMemoryTable when a DMA
 mapping insert fails

intermapRegisterDmaMapping() adds the VirtualMemory to
Device::DevMemoryTable when it registers the object's first DMA mapping,
and intermapDelDmaMapping() removes it when the last mapping goes away.
The failure path of the mapping list insert unlinked it unconditionally.
That insert can only fail on an overlap, which needs a list that already
holds mappings, so in practice the node was unlinked only by calls that
did not insert it: every "Failed to insert new mapping node" message
dropped an object with live mappings from DevMemoryTable.

When that object's last mapping was deleted later, typically while the
process exits and its client is freed, btreeUnlink() ran on a node no
longer in the tree and followed its stale parent/left/right pointers
(btreeUnlink only checks membership in checked builds). That either
oopsed in btreeUnlink at address 0x20 (NODE::parent), or left a cycle in
DevMemoryTable, and the next walk of the table spun forever under the RM
API lock, freezing every other client with nothing in the log.

Remember whether this call inserted the DevMemoryTable node and only
unlink it on the failure path in that case. Also free the new mapping
node when the DevMemoryTable insert itself fails, instead of leaking it
through NV_ASSERT_OK_OR_RETURN.

Upstream PR 1542 (brunofgmag), complementary to the partial unmap
granularity fix: that one removes a cause of the insert failures, this
one keeps any failure from corrupting DevMemoryTable. The author
reproduced the hang in a user space harness around the real btree.c and
saw 4 freezes in 12 MSFS 2024 sessions that logged the failure before,
0 in 7 after (RTX 4080, 620.70.06). Same oops as upstream issue 1540.
The leak fix is ours.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/nvidia/src/kernel/rmapi/mapping_list.c | 15 +++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/nvidia/src/kernel/rmapi/mapping_list.c b/src/nvidia/src/kernel/rmapi/mapping_list.c
index 5ff66eb6..c810c16c 100644
--- a/src/nvidia/src/kernel/rmapi/mapping_list.c
+++ b/src/nvidia/src/kernel/rmapi/mapping_list.c
@@ -175,6 +175,7 @@ intermapRegisterDmaMapping
     NV_STATUS             rmStatus = NV_OK;
     PNODE                 pNode;
     NvU64 alignment = 0;
+    NvBool                bDevMemoryTableNodeInserted = NV_FALSE;
 
     //
     // OS46_FLAGS_DMA_UNICAST_REUSE_ALLOC asked for one more mapping of a VA that
@@ -254,7 +255,14 @@ intermapRegisterDmaMapping
         pVirtualMemory->devMemoryTableNode.keyEnd = RES_GET_HANDLE(pVirtualMemory);
         pVirtualMemory->devMemoryTableNode.Data = pVirtualMemory;
 
-        NV_ASSERT_OK_OR_RETURN(btreeInsert(&pVirtualMemory->devMemoryTableNode, &pDevice->DevMemoryTable));
+        rmStatus = btreeInsert(&pVirtualMemory->devMemoryTableNode, &pDevice->DevMemoryTable);
+        if (rmStatus != NV_OK)
+        {
+            NV_ASSERT(rmStatus == NV_OK);
+            portMemFree(pNode);
+            return rmStatus;
+        }
+        bDevMemoryTableNodeInserted = NV_TRUE;
     }
 
     // register the 'dmaOffset' list itself
@@ -265,7 +273,10 @@ intermapRegisterDmaMapping
                   "Failed to insert new mapping node for range 0x%llX-0x%llX!\n",
                   pNode->keyStart, pNode->keyEnd);
         DBG_BREAKPOINT();
-        btreeUnlink(&pVirtualMemory->devMemoryTableNode, &pDevice->DevMemoryTable);
+        if (bDevMemoryTableNodeInserted)
+        {
+            btreeUnlink(&pVirtualMemory->devMemoryTableNode, &pDevice->DevMemoryTable);
+        }
         portMemFree(pNode);
         return rmStatus;
     }
